-- title:
--   Smooth-point package ascends a directed tower of constant fields
-- statement:
--   Let $k_0 \subseteq L \subseteq F$ be fields (with $k_0$ acting on $L$ and on $F$ compatibly), let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $F/k_0$ with $k_0(\operatorname{im} L) \sqcup F_0 = F$ as intermediate fields, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $L$, let $\bar F$ be a field over the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$, let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with values in $\bar F$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ meeting $L$ exactly in $A$, together with a surjection onto $\bar F$ with kernel the maximal ideal, extending the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ has an $L$-multiple with nonzero residue), and let $Q$ be a place of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$. Let $(K_n)_{n \in \iota}$ be a nonempty directed family of intermediate fields of $L/k_0$ exhausting $L$, and $A_n$ a valuation subring of $K_n$ with $A_n = A \cap K_n$. Suppose given for each $n$ a subring $S_n \subseteq F$, a ring map $\varphi_n : A_n[T] \to S_n$, a character $\chi_n : S_n \to \kappa$ and a set $D_n$ of places of $F/L$ such that: the residue field of $A_n$ surjects onto $\kappa$; the image of $A_n$ in $F$ lies in $S_n$; $\varphi_n$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_n(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in $F$ and $\chi_n\varphi_n(C\,a)$ the residue of $a$, while $\chi_n\varphi_n(T) = 0$; for each $c \in A_n$ with residue $0$ there is a unique $A_n$-section $\chi : S_n \to A_n$ of $\varphi_n \circ C$ whose residue is $\chi_n$ and which sends $\varphi_n(T)$ to $c$; every element of $S_n$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in $Q$, and the $Q$-residue of that is the image of its $\chi_n$-value; $\varphi_n(T)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has $Q$-order $1$; $D_n$ consists exactly of the places $P$ with $\operatorname{algebraMap} L \to P.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ surjective, with $S_n$ contained in the valuation ring of $P$ and all values $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of elements of $S_n$ in $A$, and with $|P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f| < 1$ for the valuation of $A$ exactly when $\chi_n f = 0$; each $A_n$-section of $\varphi_n \circ C$ inducing $\chi_n$ arises from a unique $P \in D_n$ via $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$; for $P \in D_n$ and $f$ in the level-$n$ field $k_0(\operatorname{im} K_n) \sqcup F_0$, membership of $f$ in the valuation ring of $P$ is equivalent to $f$ being a quotient $g/h$ of elements of $S_n$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,h \neq 0$; a nonzero $f$ of that level-$n$ field with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f = 0$ for all $P \in D_n$ becomes a unit of $S_n$ after multiplication by a nonzero element of $K_n$; an $f$ of that field lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in all valuation rings of $D_n$ lies in $S_n$; and $S_n$ is, up to units, generated by a finite set together with the image of $A_n$. Suppose further the tower compatibilities: $S_n \subseteq S_{n'}$ and $S_{n'} \subseteq \langle S_n, \operatorname{im} A_{n'} \rangle$ whenever $K_n \le K_{n'}$, the parameters $\varphi_n(T)$ all agree in $F$, and $\chi_{n'}$ restricts to $\chi_n$ on $S_n$. Then there exist a subring $S \subseteq F$, a map $\varphi : A[T] \to S$, a character $\chi_0 : S \to \kappa$ and a set $D$ of places of $F/L$ such that $S$ contains every $S_n$ and is their union, $\varphi(T)$ equals every $\varphi_n(T)$, $\chi_0$ restricts to each $\chi_n$, $D = D_n$ for every $n$, and $(S, \varphi, \chi_0, D)$ satisfies all the clauses above at level $A$: the image of $A$ lies in $S$, $\varphi$ is formally smooth and formally unramified with $\varphi(C\,a)$ the image of $a$, $\chi_0 \varphi(C\,a)$ the residue of $a$ and $\chi_0 \varphi(T) = 0$; unique $A$-sections for each $c \in A$ of residue $0$; $R$ reads $\chi_0$ at $Q$ and $\varphi(T)$ has $Q$-order $1$; the same description of $D$ by rationality, integrality of values and the condition $|{\cdot}| < 1 \iff \chi_0 = 0$; the bijection between $A$-sections and places of $D$; and — now for all $f \in F$, without any level restriction — the quotient description of the valuation ring of each $P \in D$, the statement that a nonzero $f$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f = 0$ throughout $D$ becomes a unit of $S$ after multiplication by a nonzero element of $L$, and the statement that $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ lying in all valuation rings of $D$ lies in $S$.
--
--   This is the limit step for smooth-point charts: a chart of a curve over the residue disc of a point, given over each member of a directed family of fields of constants exhausting $L$, ascends to a chart over the full valuation ring $A$, and the residue discs at the finite levels all coincide with the limit disc. It is used by the constructions of Igusa-style smooth-point charts on modular curves of full level, which supply the per-level packages and their tower compatibilities.
